# S12.1 final review: pre-marker barrier recovery journal

Date: 2026-09-30
Scope: Control PR #203, final same-SHA review P1

## Finding

Repository-root ownership and `.git` exchange could begin before the durable
deployment-attempt marker. A host or controller crash in that interval could
leave a root-only checkout or exchanged Git directory without a durable index
that the recovery command knew how to consume.

## Correction

Before any parent/root chmod or `.git` exchange, the controller now writes a
root-private durable journal containing only the exact repository parent,
checkout and Git-directory ownership/modes. The shared parent is locked as
part of the same recovery barrier, closing rename/replacement of the canonical
roots and disposable fetch stage.

If no deployment-attempt marker exists, `recover` performs barrier-only
recovery, removes the fixed disposable stage and reports zero rollbacks. If the
attempt marker exists, rollback validates or creates the same journal and
removes it only after repository and parent metadata are durably restored. A
deploy invocation that discovers an orphan journal recovers it and stops; it
never continues into a second attempt.

## Safety

The journal contains no tokens, credential values, Telegram content, identity
material or provider payload. This is a source-only correction; no server
deployment is performed until CI and final same-SHA review are green.
